 "notes": "E259 is the excavation row for the unit's site (0 m, bearing invalid), coded grid E259. The 'small baptistarium' (Finkelstein p. 536) was not coded as a pool (a font, no size or basin named). Burial caves 'in the northern slope (to Wadi el-'Asas)' coded direction N from the unit; the MB-dated cave is coded separately (it is one of them). E261, S1934/E262 list no pool, pit or grave. SWP: Khurbet el Khudriyeh (Ns) is the unit ('Traces of ruins', no features). El Khudr (Nr), also linked in Stage 1b, appears to be a different place: it is located 'East of the village of Taiyibeh', lies in a different square, has a standing Crusader chapel and a modern Christian graveyard, and no WBADB row within 2 km matches it; ignored (its cisterns, cave, shafts and tombs are not coded)."
